# Android Safe Deploy Rule

When deploying to a connected Android phone, protect local app data.

- Never run uninstall-based flows (`flutter install`, `adb uninstall`, or any flow that uninstalls first).
- Always use in-place install only: `adb install -r`.
- Do not switch build/signing variants without explicit user confirmation, because mismatch can force uninstall.
- If in-place install fails due to signature mismatch (`INSTALL_FAILED_UPDATE_INCOMPATIBLE`), stop and ask the user.
- If needed, build first, then install the exact built APK with `-r`.

Preferred commands:

```bash
flutter build apk --debug
adb -s <device_id> install -r build/app/outputs/flutter-apk/app-debug.apk
```

Use `tools/safe_install_android.sh` when available.
